I've added the ScopeProvider to wrap the CommentComponent. The ScopeProvider will provide the necessary context that the useScope hook requires. The error was occurring because the component tree was trying to use the useScope hook without having access to the ScopeProvider context.

Note that in a real application, the ScopeProvider would typically be higher up in the component tree and would have actual organization/scope data from the router. For the preview environment, we're just providing the basic provider wrapper to satisfy the context requirement.

